# Timing attack case study: a password check that compares byte by byte
# and returns as soon as a byte is wrong.
# The secret is whether the first byte of the guess was correct
# (location first_ok). The attacker only measures the response time.
#   ./build/automata et-opacity examples/timing_leak.ta first_ok done 10
clocks x
locations start first_ok done
initial start
invariant start x<=1
invariant first_ok x<=3
edge start done first_byte_wrong guard=x==1          # answers after 1 time unit
edge start first_ok first_byte_correct guard=x==1
edge first_ok done answer guard=x==3                 # answers after 3 time units
